.TH SYLVE 1 "2026-10-28" "sylve-cli @VERSION@" "General Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
sylve \- manage Sylve FreeBSD clusters, virtual machines, jails, storage,
and networking
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sylve
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sylve
is the command-line client for Sylve. It stores a bearer token in the active
context and sends it to the selected Sylve node.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Path to the CLI configuration file.
Default:
.I ~/.config/sylve/config.yaml
.TP
.BR \-\-context " " \fINAME\fR
Use a named login context.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-node " " \fINODE\fR
Target a cluster node by hostname or UUID.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-insecure
Skip TLS certificate verification.
.TP
.BR \-\-timeout " " \fISECONDS\fR
HTTP request timeout. Default: 30.
.TP
.BR \-\-max\-width " " \fICOLUMNS\fR
Maximum table width. Default: terminal width.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-truncate
Wrap long table cells instead of truncating them.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the CLI version and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Authentication and configuration
.TP
.BR "login " [\fISERVER\fR] " [" \-u " " USER "]" " [" \-p " " PASSWORD "]"
Authenticate and save a context.
.TP
.BR "logout"
Revoke the current token and clear it from the active context.
.TP
.BR "whoami"
Show the authenticated user and token status.
.TP
.BR "config " \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
View or edit contexts. Subcommands:
.BR view ", " get\-contexts ", " use\-context ", " set\-node ", \
" delete\-context .
.SS Resource commands
.TP
.BR "cluster " \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Show cluster status and resources; create, join, or leave a cluster;
manage notes.
.TP
.BR "node " \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
List nodes, show telemetry, drain a node, reboot it, remove a peer, or
read audit logs.
.TP
.BR "vm " \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
List, create, inspect, start, stop, migrate, snapshot, template, and
configure VMs.
.TP
.BR "jail " \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
List, create, inspect, start, stop, migrate, snapshot, template, and
configure jails.
.TP
.BR "network " \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Manage interfaces, switches, routes, DHCP, PF firewall, objects, and WireGuard.
.TP
.BR "download " \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
List, start, upload, delete, and download ISO or disk images.
.TP
.BR "replication " \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Manage HA replication policies and events.
.TP
.BR "backup " \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Manage backup targets, jobs, snapshots, and events.
.TP
.BR "zfs " \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Manage pools, datasets, snapshots, periodic snapshots, and dashboard data.
.TP
.BR "task " \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Inspect, wait for, or cancel guest lifecycle and migration tasks.
.SS Host and identity commands
.TP
.BR "system " \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Manage disks, SMART tests, PCI passthrough, files, certificates, settings,
services, tunables, host notes, and health checks.
.TP
.BR "samba " \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Manage Samba configuration and shares.
.TP
.BR "iscsi " \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Manage iSCSI targets, initiators, LUNs, and portals.
.TP
.BR "ddns " \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Manage dynamic DNS entries.
.TP
.BR "mdns " \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Manage mDNS configuration and records.
.TP
.BR "notifications " \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Manage notification transports, rules, and active notifications.
.TP
.BR "user " \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Manage local, PAM, and imported users, plus passkeys.
.TP
.BR "group " \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Manage authentication groups and membership.
.TP
.BR "auth " \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Inspect login configuration, create SSE tokens, and use passkeys.
.TP
.BR "cloud-init " \fISUBCOMMAND\fR
Manage reusable cloud-init templates.
.SH "WRITE COMMANDS"
Commands with generic API access accept:
.TP
.BR \-\-data " " \fIDATA\fR
JSON or YAML request body, or
.I @FILE
to read it from disk.
.TP
.BR \-\-param " " \fIKEY=VALUE\fR
Query parameter. Repeat for multiple parameters.
.PP
Destructive commands prompt for confirmation on a terminal. Use
.B \-y
or
.B \-\-yes
to skip the prompt.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sylve login https://sylve.example.test
sylve node list
sylve vm list -f json
sylve vm show 101
sylve vm create web-01 --pool zroot --memory 2G --disk-size 20G
sylve vm create --template debian-13 --rid 120 --start --wait
sylve jail list -f table
sylve system disk-list
sylve system cert-list
sylve download list --long
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sylve/config.yaml
CLI contexts and session tokens.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SYLVE_CONFIG
Configuration file path.
.TP
.B SYLVE_CONTEXT
Active context name.
.TP
.B SYLVE_SERVER
Server URL override.
.TP
.B SYLVE_TOKEN
Bearer token override.
.TP
.B SYLVE_NODE
Default target node.
.TP
.B SYLVE_INSECURE
Set to 1, true, or yes to skip TLS verification.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR sylve-config (5)
.SH NOTES
Manpage source:
.I docs/man/src/sylve.1.in
.br
Update the source when the CLI changes, then regenerate with:
.B make man
